---
.title = "WebRTC: peer-to-peer for the browser",
.description = "WebRTC carries a glowcap session over an encrypted DataChannel, with direct browser-to-browser channels after signaling.",
.date = .date("2026-07-22T00:00:00"),
.layout = "page.shtml",
.draft = false,
---

WebRTC carries glowcap between browsers over a direct
[WebRTC](https://www.w3.org/TR/webrtc/) DataChannel, encrypted with DTLS, with
no server on the byte path. A WebRTC peer has no address to dial, so both ends
arrange the connection through a capability they can already reach.

# Dial

TypeScript has a managed connector. The Zig, Python, Rust, and Racket tabs are
marked `PLANNED`: each exposes the lower-level pieces, but not the managed
adapter the tab shows.

